            "review_text": "jamesbn2017\nHalifax, Canada17 contributions\n0\nBusy & noisy, good but pricey seafood.\nMar 2017 • Couples\nThis is a big modern restaurant that specializes in seafood, and has a wall of salt water aquariums holding fresh fish and seafood. Our server spoke very little English and the entire menu is not translated so ordering was a bit of a challenge, but we were able to get what we ordered. Unfortunately they allow smoking, and despite what I assume to be modern ventilation, the smoke still travels. The Tom Yum soup was disappointing with a dozen pieces of large ginger throughout. The salmon is sold by the kilogram and all you get on your plate is the salmon, (not trimmed of all the fat), and a little slaw salad on the side. The shrimp salad rolls were very good.\nRead more\nWritten March 3, 2017",
